Correction to F-4958 (J-3950): the sentence "the 288 logged 0.0 rows are those with EMPTY evidence" overreaches. The evidence field is only logged on the 85 rows with judge_status=ok (newer schema); the other 683 rows have no evidence field at all, so evidence status of the older 244 zeros is unknown. What is established: among the rows that do log evidence, the 44 exact-0.0 rows ALL have empty evidence and every row with non-empty evidence scored above 0 (perfect separation, 0 exceptions), and replay of those 44 gives 0.0 on 220/220 calls under all five prefill variants. The extension to the older 244 zero rows is inferred, not verified. The rest of F-4958 stands.
